 # seen here: the estimate errs towards not yielding).  Only while the read has STRATA_YIELD_MIN_LEFT tokens left
 # (default 4 x STRATA_YIELD_SHORT, at least 1024), at most STRATA_YIELDS_MAX times per request (default 2), asked again
-# STRATA_YIELD_RETRY_S after the engine answered YIELDNO (default 2).  A read that may give way takes a slot the engine can
-# keep it in (INFO yield_row=k: b % k == k - 1, the top row of a pipelined group), the one that widens its group least
-# (STRATA_YIELD_TOP_ROW=0: the usual slot choice, and such a read does not give way unless it lands there).
+# STRATA_YIELD_RETRY_S after the engine answered `YIELDNO <slot> later` (default 2; `final`: not again for this request).
+# Every request takes the usual slot (lanes, holes); the part read waits in a free slot the engine can keep it in (INFO
+# yield_row=k: b % k == k - 1, the top row of a pipelined group, which no pad row writes), reserved only while the read
+# is paused, and the resumed BGEN names it (yslot=<b>).  A paused read takes the control lines back only once no
+# waiting request is short any more (or after STRATA_ADMIT_MAX_WAIT_S), so a burst of short requests all goes first.
 YIELD_SHORT = max(0, _int_env("STRATA_YIELD_SHORT", 0))
 YIELD_MIN_LEFT = max(1, _int_env("STRATA_YIELD_MIN_LEFT", max(1024, 4 * YIELD_SHORT)))
 YIELDS_MAX_ENV = max(0, _int_env("STRATA_YIELDS_MAX", 2))
